          "text": "The pattern indexes as a monoclinic double-perovskite cell:\n\n- \\(a \\approx 5.5022\\) \u00c5\n- \\(b \\approx 5.7271\\) \u00c5\n- \\(c \\approx 7.8971\\) \u00c5\n- \\(\\beta \\approx 90.25^\\circ\\)\n- \\(Z=2\\)\n\nThe diagnostic \\(010\\), \\(020\\), and \\(030\\) reflections occur near 15.46\u00b0, 31.21\u00b0, and 47.59\u00b0, respectively, excluding the usual \\(P2_1/n\\) model. The absence of \\(100\\) and \\(001\\), while \\(101\\) is present, is consistent with an \\(n\\)-glide. The best symmetry assignment is therefore the nonstandard \\(P\\,1\\,2/n\\,1\\) setting of space group No. 13. Mg/Nb are ordered, while Ca/Sm share the A site statistically.\n\nThe oxygen and displacement parameters below are a chemically constrained powder solution and should be treated as starting values for final Rietveld refinement.\n\n```cif\ndata_CaSmMgNbO6\n_audit_creation_method             'Powder indexing and constrained double-perovskite model'\n_chemical_name_common              'calcium samarium magnesium niobate'\n_chemical_formula_structural       'CaSmMgNbO6'\n_chemical_formula_sum              'Ca Sm Mg Nb O6'\n_chemical_formula_weight           403.64\n_cell_formula_units_Z              2\n\n_diffrn_radiation_type             'Cu Kalpha1'\n_diffrn_radiation_wavelength       1.5406\n\n_space_group_crystal_system        monoclinic\n_space_group_name_H-M_alt          'P 1 2/n 1'\n_space_group_IT_number             13\n\n_cell_length_a                     5.5022(5)\n_cell_length_b                     5.7271(5)\n_cell_length_c                     7.8971(7)\n_cell_angle_alpha                  90\n_cell_angle_beta                   90.25(2)\n_cell_angle_gamma                  90\n_cell_volume                       248.85(5)\n\n_exptl_crystal_density_diffrn      5.39\n\nloop_\n_space_group_symop_id\n_space_group_symop_operation_xyz\n1  'x,y,z'\n2  '-x+1/2,y,-z+1/2'\n3  '-x,-y,-z'\n4  'x+1/2,-y,z+1/2'\n\nloop_\n_atom_type_symbol\n_atom_type_oxidation_number\nCa  2\nSm  3\nMg  2\nNb  5\nO  -2\n\nloop_\n_atom_site_label\n_atom_site_type_symbol\n_atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity\n_atom_site_fract_x\n_atom_site_fract_y\n_atom_site_fract_z\n_atom_site_occupancy\n_atom_site_B_iso_or_equiv\nCaA   Ca  4  0.7568  0.2517  0.4991  0.500  0.60\nSmA   Sm  4  0.7568  0.2517  0.4991  0.500  0.45\nMgB   Mg  2  0.2500  0.2475  0.2500  1.000  0.45\nNbB   Nb  2  0.2500  0.2570  0.7500  1.000  0.35\nO1    O   4  0.2675  0.2510  0.5008  1.000  0.85\nO2    O   4  0.4930  0.5200  0.2470  1.000  0.85\nO3    O   4  0.5070  0.0200  0.2530  1.000  0.85\n```\n\nA triclinic \\(P\\overline1\\) A-site-ordered derivative is the only meaningful lower-symmetry alternative, but it is not favored because it should generate additional odd-axis reflections, particularly near the missing \\(100\\) position around 16.1\u00b0.",
